    "body": "The Tormach post starts the spindle for every tool, including a probe. A probing operation posts:\n\n```\nT7 M6\nG43 H7\nS0 M3\n```\n\nFound while preparing the #500 Hub check (`test-500-tormach-probe-guard.nc`). The block comes from `startPreamble()` in `assets/posts/tormach.cps` (`block([\"S\" + ni(sRpm), \"M3\"])`), which is the same on main. It is not something #500 added.\n\n**Why it matters:** a wireless touch probe must never be spun. At S0 the spindle should not turn, but the program still commands it on. That relies on the control treating S0 as stopped, and any spindle-override or minimum-RPM behaviour turns it into a spinning probe. A probe tool should get no `S`/`M3` at all, and an `M5` if the previous tool left the spindle running.\n\n**Check the other posts too:** fanuc, haas, mazak, sinumerik and heidenhain may share the same pattern.\n\nDone means: a probe-tool section posts no spindle start (and stops a running spindle) in every post that handles probing, pinned by a post test on a probing program per affected post.\n",
    "closed_by": null,
